From c9ce652e7abe549ad7e1920f03afd0d1d7bf6689 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman Fries <baracoder@googlemail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:28:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add: workspace switching via ext-workspace

Bars and docks (waybar, Quickshell-based shells) bind
ext_workspace_manager_v1 to list workspaces and switch between them.

A desktop spans every output, so each desktop is a workspace in a
single group that every output enters, in desktop order with its index
as its coordinate. The active desktop is the active workspace, and a
desktop holding an urgent window is urgent. Clients can activate,
remove (refused, as from Python, for the last or a non-empty desktop)
and create desktops.

The state is published once per main-loop iteration as a diff against
what each client was last sent, rather than from every site that can
rename, reorder, switch or mark a desktop urgent, or add an output.
